## Building a Quiz Game

### Question Structure

```xiom
type Question {
  text: Str;
  correct_answer: Str;
  points: Int;
}

fn create_questions() -> Vec[Question] {
  let mut questions: Vec[Question] = Vec[Question].new();
  questions.push(Question{ text: "What is 2 + 2?", correct_answer: "4", points: 10 });
  questions.push(Question{ text: "Capital of France?", correct_answer: "Paris", points: 10 });
  questions.push(Question{ text: "Red + Blue = ?", correct_answer: "Purple", points: 10 });
  questions
}
```

### Running a Quiz

```xiom
fn run_quiz(questions: &Vec[Question]) -> Int {
  let mut score = 0;
  let mut correct = 0;
  let mut i = 0;

  while i < questions.len() {
    let q = questions.get(i).unwrap();
    io.println(q.text);

    let user_answer = "4";

    if user_answer == q.correct_answer {
      io.println("Correct!");
      score += q.points;
      correct += 1;
    } else {
      io.println("Wrong!");
    };
    i += 1;
  };

  io.println(correct);
  io.println(score);
  score
}
```

### Calculating Grade

```xiom
fn calculate_grade(score: Int, max_score: Int) -> Str {
  let pct = score * 100 / max_score;
  if pct >= 90 { return "A"; };
  if pct >= 80 { return "B"; };
  if pct >= 70 { return "C"; };
  if pct >= 60 { return "D"; };
  "F"
}
```

### Results Summary

```xiom
fn show_results(correct: Int, total: Int, score: Int) {
  let grade = calculate_grade(score, total * 10);
  io.println(correct);
  io.println(total);
  io.println(grade);
}
```

